# Brief Cloud - local env. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. (.env* is gitignored.)

# ── Clerk (login + profile) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clerk dashboard → API keys
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up

# ── Supabase (Postgres + Storage only; no Supabase Auth) ─────────────────
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...        # service_role secret (server-only)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...  # only if a browser client is needed (likely not)

# ── OpenAI (ticket-filing agent + audio transcription) ───────────────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# AGENT_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna            # optional; writes + files tickets (default in lib/agent/model.ts)
# AGENT_FAST_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna       # optional; the in-page ticket assistant
# TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-4o-transcribe  # optional; default in code (gpt-4o-transcribe)

# ── App ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Tracker connections ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Brief runs every tracker's OAuth flow and stores the tokens encrypted in
# tracker_connections. A provider left blank shows as unavailable in Settings,
# except Linear, Jira and GitHub, which then connect through Clerk as they did
# before moving to Brief's OAuth. Each app's redirect URI is
# <APP_URL>/api/connect/<provider>/callback (TRACKERS.md).
#
# Token encryption key, base64 of 32 random bytes. Changing it orphans every
# stored connection. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
CONNECTIONS_KEY=
# Linear: Settings > API > OAuth applications, public (Client ID, Client secret)
LINEAR_CLIENT_ID=
LINEAR_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Jira: an Atlassian OAuth 2.0 (3LO) app of its own for dev, since an app holds one callback URL
JIRA_CLIENT_ID=
JIRA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GitHub: an OAuth App (not a GitHub App) with the localhost callback (Client ID, client secret)
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GitLab: a gitlab.com application, confidential, scopes api and read_user (Application ID, Secret)
GITLAB_CLIENT_ID=
GITLAB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Azure DevOps: an Entra ID app registration (Application ID, client secret Value)
AZURE_DEVOPS_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_DEVOPS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ClickUp: Settings > Apps > Create new app
CLICKUP_CLIENT_ID=
CLICKUP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Notion: a public integration, Configuration tab (OAuth Client ID, OAuth Client Secret)
NOTION_CLIENT_ID=
NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Trello: the Power-Up's API key (its token flow needs no secret)
TRELLO_API_KEY=
# Trello: the Power-Up's secret, unused by the token flow
# TRELLO_API_SECRET=
# Asana: developer console app (Client ID, Client secret)
ASANA_CLIENT_ID=
ASANA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Asana: space-separated scopes, only when the app uses specific scopes instead of Full permissions
# ASANA_SCOPES=
# Monday: Developer Center app, Basic Information (Client ID, Client Secret)
MONDAY_CLIENT_ID=
MONDAY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Clerk tracker connections, from before the move to Brief's OAuth ─────
# Linear, Jira and GitHub connected through Clerk still file until their users
# reconnect, and a deployment without the app secrets above still connects
# them through Clerk. Only set these to point one at a CUSTOM Clerk connector
# (a paid feature on production instances). They go with the Clerk path
# (TRACKERS.md, "Cleanup after migration").
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_CLERK_STRATEGY=oauth_custom_<slug>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINEAR_CLERK_STRATEGY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_JIRA_CLERK_STRATEGY=
#
# A basic-auth Jira test account, used when nothing else holds Jira.
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=
# JIRA_EMAIL=
# JIRA_SITE=https://<site>.atlassian.net

# ── Live tracker tests (lib/<provider>.e2e.test.ts) ──────────────────────
# Each suite is skipped unless its token is set. Personal tokens, never an app
# secret; TRACKERS.md says how to make each one. Run from web/ with:
#   node --env-file=.env.local node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run lib/<provider>.e2e.test.ts
# Every *_TARGET is optional; without it the first target the token sees is used.
# Azure DevOps: a PAT, and the organization name from dev.azure.com/<org>
# LIVE_AZURE_PAT=
# LIVE_AZURE_ORG=
# Azure DevOps: project name or id
# LIVE_AZURE_TARGET=
# ClickUp: a personal pk_ token, and a list id
# LIVE_CLICKUP_TOKEN=
# LIVE_CLICKUP_TARGET=
# Trello: an API key and a token made for it, and a board id
# LIVE_TRELLO_KEY=
# LIVE_TRELLO_TOKEN=
# LIVE_TRELLO_TARGET=
# Notion: an internal integration secret shared with a database, and that database id
# LIVE_NOTION_TOKEN=
# LIVE_NOTION_TARGET=
# GitLab: a personal access token with the api scope, and a project id
# LIVE_GITLAB_TOKEN=
# LIVE_GITLAB_TARGET=
# Asana: a personal access token, a workspace gid and a project gid
# LIVE_ASANA_TOKEN=
# LIVE_ASANA_WORKSPACE=
# LIVE_ASANA_TARGET=
# Monday: a personal API token, and a board id
# LIVE_MONDAY_TOKEN=
# LIVE_MONDAY_TARGET=
